How many borns in a human body?  At birth the human body has about 350 bones, but by the time adulthood rolls around, some of our bones have fused together to give us a total of 206 bones in our body!

Here is the breakdown:

The adult skeleton consists of 206 bones . . . 

- 28 skull bones (8 cranial, 14 facial, and 6 ear bones); 

- the horseshoe-shaped hyoid bone of the neck; 

- 26 vertebrae (7 cervical or neck, 12 thorax, 5 lumbar or loins, the sacrum which is five fused vertebrae, and the coccyx, our vestigial tail, which is four fused vertebrae);

- 24 ribs plus the sternum or breastbone; the shoulder girdle (2 clavicles, the most frequently fractured bone in the body, and 2 scapulae); 

- the pelvic girdle (2 fused bones); 

- 30 bones in our arms and legs (a total of 120); 

- There are also a few partial bones, ranging from 8-18 in number, which are related to joints.

How do you calculate 2*3 using a slide rule?  Specifically, I do not know.  However the principal of a slide rule is that it utilizes natural logs of numbers.  Specifically, the natural log of the product of two numbers is the inverse log of the sum of the two logs... or, in normal terms...

ln(a*b) = exp( ln(a) + ln(b) );

So the way to do this on a slide rule is to add the two natural logs together and then calculate the inverse..

SOS Help Me C programing!!? Write a function that removes all whitespaces from a string. You MUST use strtok( ) and strcat( ) to remove whitespaces. No other string library functions you can use.
void RemoveWhiteSpaces(char *string); void RemoveWhiteSpaces(char *string) {
char * bch;
char newstr[80];
// Get the first whitespace
bch = strtok (string,' ');

while (*bch != '&#92;0')
{
  if(string != ' ') {
   strcat(newstr,bch);
  }
  *bch++;
}

return 0;
}


